cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Yuzen: a thin liquid film flow solver based on the lubrication approximation"
message: "If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shiratori
    given-names: Suguru
    email: sshrator@tcu.ac.jp
    affiliation: "Tokyo City University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0158-6798"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sugurushiratori/Yuzen"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23502846
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23502846
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions of Yuzen (resolves to the latest)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23502847
    description: "Yuzen 1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Yuzen solves the long-wave (lubrication) equation for the height of a thin
  liquid film on a substrate, coupled to a transport equation for the solute
  concentration. It covers capillary leveling, disjoining pressure and the
  contact line, solutal (Marangoni) stresses, evaporation and the resulting
  viscosity rise, gravity, centrifugal force and substrate topography, in one
  and two horizontal dimensions. The height equation is advanced with a
  Newton-Kantorovich iteration and Crank-Nicolson in time; the two equations
  are coupled by block Gauss-Seidel so that the converged state is the fully
  implicit coupled solution. With the Eigen backend, results are
  bit-identical regardless of the OpenMP thread count, and the test suite
  asserts it.
keywords:
  - thin liquid film
  - lubrication approximation
  - long-wave equation
  - coating flow
  - spin coating
  - wetting
  - dewetting
  - contact line
  - disjoining pressure
  - Marangoni
  - evaporation
  - computational fluid dynamics
